From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 17:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci-plat: mark streams broken on Amlogic G12 DWC3 hosts

The DWC3-based xHCI on Amlogic G12-family SoCs (G12A/G12B/SM1) wedges
under concurrent bulk-stream traffic: with a UAS mass-storage device
issuing bursts of small sync writes across ~30 streams, transfer
completions silently stop while control transfers continue, the
subsequent Stop Endpoint command never completes, and the controller is
declared dead (xhci_hc_died), taking down both buses.  Reproduced in
~3 minutes with an ext4 root on a UAS SSD running dpkg; identical
hardware running the same workload over usb-storage (BOT) on the same
SuperSpeed link survives indefinitely.

Set XHCI_BROKEN_STREAMS for hosts descending from
"amlogic,meson-g12a-usb-ctrl", and add a generic
"xhci-broken-streams-quirk" device property (readable from DT or ACPI
_DSD, matching the existing quirk properties) so firmware can declare
the same fact.  With streams marked broken, uas falls back to
usb-storage automatically.

Signed-off-by: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c	2026-09-02 17:30:00.000000000 -0700
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-plat.c	2026-09-02 17:30:00.000000000 -0700
@@ -277,6 +277,22 @@
 		if (device_property_read_bool(tmpdev, "xhci-skip-phy-init-quirk"))
 			xhci->quirks |= XHCI_SKIP_PHY_INIT;
 
+		if (device_property_read_bool(tmpdev, "xhci-broken-streams-quirk"))
+			xhci->quirks |= XHCI_BROKEN_STREAMS;
+
+		/*
+		 * The DWC3 xHCI on Amlogic G12-family SoCs wedges its command
+		 * ring under concurrent bulk-stream traffic (UAS sync-write
+		 * bursts): stream completions stop, Stop Endpoint never
+		 * completes and the host is declared dead.  Streams cannot be
+		 * used safely on this controller; uas then binds storage via
+		 * usb-storage (BOT) instead.
+		 */
+		if (tmpdev->of_node &&
+		    of_device_is_compatible(tmpdev->of_node,
+					    "amlogic,meson-g12a-usb-ctrl"))
+			xhci->quirks |= XHCI_BROKEN_STREAMS;
+
 		device_property_read_u32(tmpdev, "imod-interval-ns",
 					 &xhci->imod_interval);
 		device_property_read_u16(tmpdev, "num-hc-interrupters",
